---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page
  title="FTC affiliate disclosure"
  description="SoftenerIndex advertising disclosure: /go links, placeholder partners, and how commissions will be labeled if a partnership goes live."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="kicker">Legal</p>
      <h1>FTC disclosure</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        SoftenerIndex is published by Bob Molina. This page is the advertising disclosure for
        affiliate and sponsored links.
      </p>
      <h2>Material connections</h2>
      <p>
        Some outbound links on SoftenerIndex are reserved affiliate routes under
        <code>/go/…</code>. If a partner relationship is active, Molina may receive a
        commission if you click and later purchase. That does not change the editorial rule
        that hardness, installer rosters, and prices must be sourced — commissions are not a
        reason to invent a number.
      </p>
      <h2>Placeholders</h2>
      <p>
        Slugs such as <a href="/go/home-water-test">/go/home-water-test</a> and
        <a href="/go/compare-local-quotes">/go/compare-local-quotes</a> currently use
        <code>status: placeholder</code> and point at <code>example.com</code>. Those are not
        live offers, not endorsements, and not installer referrals. The interstitial on each
        <code>/go</code> page states the partner field, the disclosure text from frontmatter,
        and a sponsored/nofollow continue link.
      </p>
      <h2>How we label</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>In-article affiliate modules say “Affiliate link” and placeholder vs sponsored.</li>
        <li>Continue buttons on <code>/go</code> pages use <code>rel="sponsored nofollow noopener noreferrer"</code>.</li>
        <li>The site footer repeats a short disclosure on every page.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What we do not sell from this page</h2>
      <p>
        SoftenerIndex does not sell water-softener equipment from this disclosure. City
        installer arrays are independent of <code>/go</code> and remain empty until a named
        public source supports a row.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>
